diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index f13634a..1d433b8 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 - `Schedule.cancel(appointment_id)` marks an appointment `cancelled` instead of deleting it; cancelled appointments no longer block their slot. Stored in JSON as `status` (files without it load as `booked`).
 - `Schedule.week(therapist, monday)` returns a therapist's non-cancelled appointments for the week as a dict keyed by each date (all seven days, empty lists included), sorted by start time.
 - New client register in `clients.py`: `Client` dataclass and `ClientBook` with `add(client)` and `find_by_phone(phone)`. Phone numbers are normalized, so `079 123 45 67`, `+41 79 123 45 67` and `0041791234567` all find the same client. Adding a phone number that is already registered raises `ValueError`.
+- `Schedule.reschedule(appointment_id, new_start)` moves an appointment to a new start time, keeping its treatment. The same checks as `book` apply (opening hours, therapist overlap and turnaround gap), ignoring the appointment's own old time. A refused move leaves the appointment unchanged; cancelled appointments cannot be moved.
 - `ClientBook.search(text)` returns clients whose name contains `text`, ignoring case, in the order they were added; a blank query returns `[]`.
 
 ## 0.1.0
